WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.620
Can a process run without the cell around it?

2
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:12.980
Before 1897, many held that fermentation was tied to living yeast.

3
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:16.920
Yeast cells were thought too small to be broken open.

4
00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:22.800
Vitalists held that the chemistry of life was inseparable from the intact cell.

5
00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:25.220
A cell has many parts.

6
00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.900
Which does a process need, and which are enough?

7
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.620
Buchner broke the cells.

8
00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:37.540
He ground brewer's yeast with quartz sand and diatomite, then squeezed it in a

9
00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:43.360
hydraulic press. A thousand grams of yeast gave about 500 cc of juice.

10
00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.140
That juice fermented sugar with no living cells.

11
00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:52.480
Next, show the activity runs in the crude extract, and give it a number.

12
00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:55.553
Next, split the extract.

13
00:00:56.153 --> 00:00:57.233
A column can do it.

14
00:00:58.113 --> 00:01:03.953
In a lysate of reticulocytes, one fraction does not bind the column: Fraction 1.

15
00:01:04.853 --> 00:01:08.213
The other is washed off with high salt: Fraction 2.

16
00:01:09.373 --> 00:01:13.013
Neither supports ATP-dependent protein breakdown alone.

17
00:01:14.253 --> 00:01:16.073
Combined, they restore that activity.

18
00:01:16.917 --> 00:01:19.477
Now test one part at a time.

19
00:01:20.197 --> 00:01:24.177
Remove one protein with an antibody, and the activity is lost.

20
00:01:25.217 --> 00:01:27.757
Add the pure protein back, and it returns.

21
00:01:28.897 --> 00:01:30.697
The last test is to rebuild.

22
00:01:31.637 --> 00:01:38.897
Mix only purified parts: for E. coli mismatch repair, eight proteins, with ATP and

23
00:01:38.897 --> 00:01:43.157
dNTPs. If the reaction runs, those parts are enough.

24
00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:51.270
Cytosol from growing cells plus dATP starts parts of the apoptotic program.

25
00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:57.890
Fractionation gave a 15-kilodalton protein, which proved to be cytochrome c.

26
00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:01.390
Immunodepleting it diminished the activity.

27
00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:04.850
Adding cytochrome c back restored it.

28
00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:10.510
Diminished when removed, restored when added back: the protein is needed.

29
00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.000
Two things can mislead.

30
00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:16.760
A few living cells might survive in the juice.

31
00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:22.960
They were too few: a control with ten times as many cells as the juice held gave no

32
00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:28.180
fermentation. Killed dried yeast, called zymin, still fermented.

33
00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:33.340
Second, how you prepare an extract changes what it contains.

34
00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:39.780
In Wang's system, sucrose added to stabilize mitochondria diminished the apoptotic

35
00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:45.620
activity. Intact mitochondria likely held back the cytochrome c that was part of it.

36
00:02:46.433 --> 00:02:52.793
In the 1950s, Sutherland and Rall found that a hormone response survived breaking

37
00:02:52.793 --> 00:02:57.353
the cells. It split into a membrane step and a soluble step.

38
00:02:57.873 --> 00:02:59.353
That needed broken cells.

39
00:03:00.393 --> 00:03:07.233
In 1961, Nirenberg and Matthaei added synthetic poly-U, a template no cell would

40
00:03:07.233 --> 00:03:09.453
take up, to an E. coli extract.

41
00:03:10.133 --> 00:03:13.813
It made polyphenylalanine, the first codon assignment.

42
00:03:14.717 --> 00:03:21.157
In the late 1970s, Hershko and colleagues combined fractions of reticulocyte lysate.

43
00:03:21.997 --> 00:03:25.677
Neither fraction alone gave ATP-dependent protein breakdown.

44
00:03:26.477 --> 00:03:28.017
Together they restored it.

45
00:03:28.777 --> 00:03:32.297
Only a tube lets fractions be combined and recombined.

46
00:03:33.237 --> 00:03:37.977
In 1989, Murray and Kirschner made frog egg extracts cycle.

47
00:03:38.957 --> 00:03:42.277
Destroying their messenger RNA arrested them in interphase.

48
00:03:42.917 --> 00:03:46.257
Adding cyclin messenger RNA restored the cycles.

49
00:03:47.097 --> 00:03:51.637
A tube shows what the parts can do, not that the cell uses them that way.

50
00:03:52.317 --> 00:03:56.097
A separate experiment is needed, such as a mutant or a cell test.
